================================================================================
## Fail Knowledge Graph builds on a lost triple count instead of reporting 0
================================================================================

Context:
Forward-port of the 0.8.2 hotfix (PR #201 / Reliance): Lakehouse builds that
ran past the one-hour M2M OAuth token lifetime lost the warehouse connection
while counting triples. The count swallowed the error and returned 0, so the
build finished with "VIEW created but no triples generated". 0.9.0 still had
the static ``access_token`` connect path and the same swallowed COUNT on the
Delta pipeline, ``_BuildPipeline``, and scheduled builds.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/databricks/DatabricksAuth.py
   App-mode SQL connections pass a ``credentials_provider`` whose header factory reads ``get_oauth_token()`` on every request.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/materialize.py
   New ``count_triples``: raises ``InfrastructureError`` when the count cannot run or returns no row (complies with ``src/.coding_rules.md §4``).
3. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaTripleStoreBuildPipeline.py
   Materialized builds run the CTAS first and count the Delta table afterwards; view-only builds still count the gateway VIEW first. Count errors fail the task. Extract Method: ``_build_data_relation``, ``_finish_without_triples``.
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py
   ``_count_view_triples`` delegates to ``materialize.count_triples``. Post-sync count stays non-fatal and does not publish "Synced 0 triples" when the count is unavailable. Extract Function: ``_report_post_sync_triple_count``.
5. src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py
   Scheduled full rebuilds use the same raising count; managed-synced post-count stays non-fatal.
6. tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_materialize.py
   Recording SQL client; count failures, single gateway-VIEW scan, empty-row raise.
7. tests/units/auth/test_auth.py
   App-mode params expose ``credentials_provider``; refreshed-token header factory.
8. tests/units/dtwin/test_build_pipeline_streaming.py
   A failed post-sync count does not fail a successful synced build.
9. docs/backend.md
   ``materialize.py`` row mentions ``count_triples``.

