================================================================================
## Keep live Playwright e2e authenticated on the Apps gateway
================================================================================

Context: Against ontobricks-09x, a catch-all ``page.route("**/*")`` dropped
gateway bearer headers on fetch/XHR (``TypeError: Failed to fetch``) while
``continue_(headers=)`` on those requests broke ``window.fetch``. A
session-minted OAuth token also expired mid-suite (~1h), so later tests
landed on Databricks Sign-In. Restrict intercepts to HTML navigations,
remint the bearer every 20 minutes, and isolate a health check from a
leaked ``DATABRICKS_CONFIG_PROFILE``.

Changes:

1. tests/e2e/conftest.py
   Document-only slash-redirect intercept; ``fallback()`` for non-document;
   ``_resolve_live_bearer`` remints before the Apps token dies.
2. tests/e2e/scenarios/conftest.py
   Scenario pages use the reminted bearer, not the session probe token.
3. tests/e2e/domain/test_domain_versions_cards.py
   Stub ``/settings/registry/domains`` so mocked card tests ignore registry fetch.
4. tests/e2e/dtwin/test_dtwin_flows.py
   Wait until SPARQL playground fills the default SELECT query.
5. tests/e2e/help/test_help_modal_flows.py
   Path-traversal image URL is rejected as 400 or 404.
6. tests/units/e2e/test_scenario_campaign_wiring.py
   Contracts for document continue, XHR fallback, and bearer remint.
7. tests/units/core/test_health.py
   Pin CLI profile to ``default`` so a live-run env cannot fail the unit test.
8. tests/fixtures/databricks_auth.py
   ``mint_token(..., force_refresh=)`` maps to ``databricks auth token --force-refresh``.
9. tests/e2e/navigation/test_sidebar_bottom_alignment.py
   Live mode waits for the seeded L2 rail and expects a 4px gutter (deployed chrome).

